From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 05:45:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: the ssl entries live with the ssl implementation

The stubs were in hle_net.c, so every test that includes the socket unit suddenly needed the TLS
unit at link time (dm_ssl_* unresolved). Moving the entries into hle_ssl.c, next to the code
they call, keeps the socket unit free of the dependency: t_net_tcp and t_net_udp_remote link
again without dragging SecureTransport in, and hle_net.c mentions no dm_ssl_ symbol at all.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the ssl entries were left in hle_net.c by the TLS patch, and every socket test then needed SecureTransport at link time; this moves them next to the code they call so the socket unit stands alone. Worth upstreaming even without Nextendo: it is the same separation the rest of the host uses.
Issue: none opened yet — it is a fix to the fork's own 0066, so it folds into that PR

---
 dm/host/hle_net.c | 73 -----------------------------------------------
 dm/host/hle_ssl.c | 73 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_net.c b/dm/host/hle_net.c
index 9427dd3..009083a 100644
